 Slavensky</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 10 - <a href="https://www.stephanienguyenforassembly.com/">Stephanie Nguyen</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 11 - <a href="https://www.electloriwilson.com/">Lori Wilson</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 12 - <a href="https://www.jackie4assembly.com/">Jackie Elward</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 13 - <a href="https://voteransom.com/">Rhodesia Ransom</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 14 - <a href="https://buffywicks.com/">Buffy Wicks</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 15 - <a href="https://www.anamarie4assembly.com/">Anamarie Avila Farias</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 16 - <a href="https://www.rebeccabauerkahan.com/">Rebecca Bauer-Kahan</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 17 - <a href="https://www.matthaney.com/">Matt Haney</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 18 - <a href="http://miaforassembly.org/">Mia Bonta</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 19 - <a href="https://www.votecatherinestefani.com/">Catherine Stefani</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 20 - <a href="https://www.ortegaforassembly.com/">Liz Ortega</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 21 - <a href="https://www.dianepapan.com/">Diane Papan</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 23 - <a href="https://www.voteberman.com/">Marc Berman</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 24 - <a href="https://www.votealexlee.com/">Alex Lee</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 25 - <a href="https://www.ashkalra.com/">Ash Kalra</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 26 - <a href="https://patrickahrens.com/">Patrick Ahrens</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 27 - <a href="https://www.pachecoforca.com/" target="_blank">Brian Pacheco</a> (D)<br>AD 28 - <a href="https://www.gailpellerinforassembly.com/">Gail Pellerin </a>(D)&nbsp;<br>AD 29 - <a href="https://rivasca.org/">Robert Rivas</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 30 - <a href="https://dawnaddis.org/">Dawn Addis</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 31 - <a href="https://www.pereaforassembly.com/">Annalisa Perea</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 34 - <a href="https://www.putzforassembly.com/">Randall Putz</a> (D)<br>AD 35 - <a href="https://www.andraegonzales.com/">Andrae Gonzales</a> (D)<br>AD 36 - <a href="https://www.idaforassembly.com/">Dr. Ida Obeso-Martinez</a> (D)<br>AD 37 - <a href="https://gregghart.org/">Gregg Hart</a> (D)<br>AD 38 - <a href="https://stevebennettforassembly.com/">Steve Bennett</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 40 - <a href="https://pilar4ca.com/">Pilar Schiavo</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p></div><div class="col-md-6 col-sm-12"><p>AD 42 - <a href="https://deborahkleinlopez.com/">Deborah Klein Lopez</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 43 - <a href="https://www.votecelesterodriguez.com/">Celeste Rodriguez</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 44 - <a href="https://www.votenickschultz.com/">Nick Schultz</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 46 - <a href="https://jessegabriel.com/">Jesse Gabriel</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 47 - <a href="https://www.leilanamvar.com/">Leila Namvar</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 49 - <a href="https://mikefong.org/">Mike Fong</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 50 - <a href="https://robertgarcia4ca.com/">Robert Garcia</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 51 - <a href="https://www.rickchavezzbur.com/">Rick Chavez-Zbur </a>(D)&nbsp;<br>AD 52 - <a href="https://www.jessicacaloza.com/">Jessica Caloza </a>(D)&nbsp;<br>AD 54 - <a href="https://www.markgonzalezforassembly.com/">Mark Gonzalez</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 55 - <a href="https://isaacbryanforca.com/">Isaac Bryan</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 56 - <a href="https://lisacalderon4assembly.com/">Lisa Calderon</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 57 - <a href="https://sadeforassembly.com/">Sade Elhawary</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 58 - <a href="https://www.clarissacervantes.com/">Clarissa Cervantes</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 61 - <a href="https://www.tina4ca.com/">Tina McKinnor </a>(D)&nbsp;<br>AD 62 - <a href="https://solacheforassembly.com">Jose Solache</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 65 - <a href="https://www.ayannadavis.com/" target="_blank">Dr. Ayanna Davis</a> (D)<br>AD 66 - <a href="https://www.saradeenforca.com/">Sara Deen</a> (D)<br>AD 67 - <a href="https://markpulido.com/">Mark Pulido</a> (D)<br>AD 68 - <a href="https://www.votejessielopez.com/">Jessie Lopez</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 69 - <a href="https://joshlowenthal.com/">Josh Lowenthal</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 70 - <a href="https://www.votepaulaswift.com/">Paula Swift</a> (D)<br>AD 72 - <a href="https://www.kluweoc.com/">Chris Kluwe</a> (D)<br>AD 74 - <a href="https://sergiofarias.com/">Sergio Farias</a> (D)<br>AD 76 - <a href="https://patelforassembly.com/">Darshana Patel</a> (D)<br>AD 77 - <a href="https://tashaboerner.com/">Tasha Boerner </a>(D)&nbsp;<br>AD 78 - <a href="https://voteforward.com/">Chris Ward</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 79 - <a href="https://www.lashaeforassembly.com/">LaShae Sharp-Collins</a> (D)&nbsp;<br>AD 80 - <a href="https://www.davidalvarez.com/">David Alvarez</a> (D)</p></div></div><h6>Outside California</h6><p>CSEA has made these endorsements because the policies passed in the U.S. Senate affect working families, retirees, and public servants nationwide. Supporting candidates who champion public education, retirement security, and affordable healthcare ensures a stronger future for all Americans, including our members in California and our retired members across the nation.<br><br><strong>U.S. Senate</strong><br>Alaska – <a href="https://marypeltola.com/" target="_blank">Mary Peltola</a><br>Georgia – <a href="https://electjon.com/" target="_blank">Jon Ossoff&nbsp;</a><br>Iowa – <a href="https://turek4iowa.com/" target="_blank">Josh Turek</a><br>Maine – <a href="https://www.jacksonformaine.com/" target="_blank">Troy Jackson</a><br>Michigan – <a href="https://abdulforsenate.com/" target="_blank">Abdul El-Sayed</a><br>New Hampshire – <a href="https://chrispappas.org/">Chris Pappas</a><br>North Carolina – <a href="https://roycooper.com/new-roy-cooper-files-to-run-for-united-states-senate/" target="_blank">Roy Cooper</a><br>Ohio – <a href="https://www.sherrodbrown.com/">Sherrod Brown</a><br>Texas – <a href="https://jamestalarico.com/" target="_blank">James Talarico</a></p></div>
      
