            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><h5 class="text-primary line-highlight mb-4">How CSEA's endorsement process works</h5><p>Candidates are selected by CSEA’s&nbsp;<a href="/committees/political-action-for-classified-employees-pace">Political Action for Classified Employees (PACE) Committee</a>&nbsp;for recommendation to the <a href="/about-csea/member-leadership/board-of-directors">CSEA Board of Directors</a>, with CSEA Board Members making the official endorsement. The PACE recommendations are based on candidates’ voting records, answers to CSEA’s questionnaires and candidate interviews or some combination. Candidates are rated for such recommendation based on issues of importance to CSEA, including school and community college funding, retirement benefit protections, healthcare reform, workers’ rights and other issues impacting CSEA members in their workplace.</p></div>
      
